---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { devlogPosts } from "../data/content";
---

<Base
  title="Project Cognify: Understanding Focus"
  description="Project Cognify is a student-led research project exploring how teenagers focus, why attention is so hard to sustain, and whether studying with friends can help."
>
  <header>
    <h1 class="hero-title">Project Cognify</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">
      Investigating adolescent attention in an age of engineered distraction
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="prose intro">
    <p>
      Why is it so easy to spend three hours locked into a game, but almost
      impossible to spend thirty minutes on homework? That question is where
      Project Cognify came from, and we still don't have a full answer.
    </p>
    <p>
      We're Jonathan, Jeremy, and Ryan — three high schoolers who met at a game
      jam last year and got along well enough to want to try something bigger
      afterward. This is that something.
    </p>
    <p>
      Rather than jump straight to building an app, we spent the first few
      months just trying to understand the problem: reading academic papers,
      running a survey (30 students so far), and talking to people about how
      they actually study. We let what we found push the project around
      instead of forcing it toward whatever we'd originally assumed.
    </p>
    <p>
      That turned out to matter. We went in expecting FOMO to be the main
      driver, and it wasn't — motivation and just knowing other people are
      around kept coming up instead, both in the papers and in what students
      told us.
    </p>
    <p>
      So our first prototype, <a href="/cohort">Cohort</a>, is built around a
      much narrower bet than we started with: does it help to just <em>see</em> that
      your friends are studying too, even if you're not studying together? No
      streaks, no leaderboard, nothing gamified — just presence.
    </p>
    <p>We genuinely don't know if that's enough. That's what we're testing.</p>
  </div>

  <section class="recent">
    <p class="label">Recent devlog entries</p>
    <div class="entries">
      {
        devlogPosts.slice(0, 4).map((post) => (
          <article class="entry">
            <p class="meta">
              <time datetime={post.dateISO}>{post.date}</time>
              {post.author && (
                <>
                  <span>—</span>
                  <span>{post.author}</span>
                </>
              )}
            </p>
            <h3>
              <a href={`/devlog#${post.id}`}>{post.title}</a>
            </h3>
            <p class="entry__excerpt">{post.excerpt}</p>
            <a class="link-sm" href={`/devlog#${post.id}`}>
              read more →
            </a>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .intro {
    margin: 3.5rem 0;
  }

  .intro p {
    font-size: 1.06rem;
  }

  .intro .question {
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin: 1.25rem 0;
  }

  .recent {
    margin-top: 3.5rem;
  }

  .recent .entries {
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
</style>
